                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've been playing the Atelier game since Rorona and have enjoyed the games.  Gust has been a bad influence, but up until this game in the series, the game was fair and dlc included extras (you could make or buy yourself in the game with time) or special stuff like outfits, that didnt' really matter so much, but were nice.  However, the Secret Bag and increasing the basket size has always been part of the mechanics to improve gameplay and make the game less tedious.  It was a pain that you sometimes had to be in the Atelier on the right day having had a full basket, but that can be done.  Having to pay for recipes (with real cash) after paying $40+ for the base game is ridiculous.  $79.99 for a DLC pack is beyond greedy and I will probably never buy another Atelier game and will most likely pass on anything with Gust involved now.  There are less greedy companies, wtith the gamers themselves more in mind.  If you get the game for cheap, then it's fun, but this is the grindiest of them and the reason why is they want you to pay for dlc to make the game more enjoyable.  I hope that helps.",
